{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837335-the-new-dawn-in-2e","id":837335,"title":"The New Dawn in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-25T18:22:20-08:00","id":837335,"title":"The New Dawn in 2e","content":"Consider the following tweak to 1e's Final Azoth Roll mechanics:<br /> <br /> \u2022 First, no do-overs. The Final Azoth roll truly is final. <br /> \u2023 Complete and total amnesia only occurs on a botch. <br /> \u2023 On a failure, you become an ordinary human, with selective amnesia of your time as a Promethean: you remember the broad outlines of your former existence, but reinterpret them in mundane terms. <br /> \u2023 On a success, you retain accurate memories of your former existence; additionally, you're immune to Disquiet (and, in crossover games, other similar effects that rob you of agency: the Kiss doesn't paralyze you, Lunacy doesn't terrorize you, you're a Sleepwalker, Sybaris doesn't affect you, etc.)<br /> \u2023 On an exceptional success, you also achieve a Boon. (See 1e's Redeemed Boons from the now-defunct Athanor rules for a sample of what you'd get.)<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> EDIT: the motives behind this suggestion are three-fold. <br /> <br /> 1) Streamline the Final Azoth roll \u2014 after all, there's a good chance that it doesn't get roleplayed beyond a single \u201crides into the sunset\u201d scene, so anything that requires you to make weekly rolls is counterproductive. Besides, the weekly rolls in 1e lead to a break between the fluff (which implied that most Prometheans ended up amnesiacs) and the mechanics (where a two-dice Azoth pool gave you even odds of regaining your memories, and larger pools practically guaranteed that you'd regain your memories within a couple of months, tops). <br /> <br /> 2) Bias the Final Azoth roll toward producing a human being who represents the potential humans can achieve rather than the average mortal in the Chronicles of Darkness. This is why I suggested that the failure result gives you the default mortal condition while a success gives you a mortal who doesn't need to worry about agency-robbing effects such as Disquiet. It also sets up a nice dichotomy between success and failure, where failure results in suffering something analogous to <b>Mage</b>'s Sleeping Curse while success results in being free of it. <br /> <br /> 3) Give Redeemed Boons a place in 2e. I understand why Athanors were reimagined as, in effect, magic items; but I rather liked the fact that in 1e, it was possible to get a little something extra in the New Dawn based on what the Promethean idealized about humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-26-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T00:02:24-08:00","id":837411,"title":"","content":"The assumption is that the roll cannot fail to grant mortality? I think that would work better in a chronicle with a certainty to move beyond the New Dawn, and even then it seems like a sure thing.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see Redeemed Merits. Say things like Elpis and Transmutations and Azoth trade over dot for dot for Merits. This could play to (I think it was) your idea to have a life waiting for the Redeemed. On an exceptional success, a handful of those dots could be applied to supernatural Merits too. Maybe a boon is the ability to ignore the drawbacks they incur, representing the perfected nature of the newly minted soul.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that I'd prefer a couple of options for tackling the New Dawn. The old system works fine for an open ended chronicle, but not so much if the Redeemed should stick around. Conversely, a chronicle that ends on Redemption shouldn't extend every time the character whiffs. If Pilgrimage has dramatically changed the endgame, I'd like to see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T00:03:54-08:00","id":837413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837335-the-new-dawn-in-2e?p=837411#post837411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The assumption is that the roll cannot fail to grant mortality?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Azoth roll comes <i>after</i> you've succeeded on the last Humanity roll in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T00:13:58-08:00","id":837415,"title":"","content":"Ah, right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}